**measure.cpp computes stick calibration and motion-sensor bias averages.**

## Interface

- `stick_measurer::observe_rest(stick_vector v) noexcept` accumulates rest samples for center estimation.
- `stick_measurer::observe_sweep(stick_vector v) noexcept` tracks absolute axis maxima via `std::fabs`.
- `stick_measurer::finalize() const noexcept -> stick_calibration` returns averaged centers, sweep ranges, and `drift_threshold`.
- `stick_measurer::reset() noexcept` value-resets all measurement state.
- `motion_bias_measurer::observe(const motion_sample& m) noexcept` accumulates gyro and accelerometer components.
- `motion_bias_measurer::finalize(motion_calibration& mc) const noexcept` writes component-wise means when `n_ != 0`; otherwise leaves `mc` unchanged.
- `motion_bias_measurer::reset() noexcept` value-resets all accumulators.

## Behavioral Contracts

`stick_measurer::finalize` uses `constexpr float min_range {0.1f}`; swept ranges are `std::max(max_x_, min_range)`/`std::max(max_y_, min_range)`, unswept ranges are `1.0f`, missing rest centers are `0.0f`, and `drift_threshold` is always `0.0f`. `motion_bias_measurer::finalize` computes means with `1.0 / static_cast<double>(n_)`.

## Coupling

`measure.cpp` depends on `measure.hpp`, `stick_vector`, `stick_calibration`, `motion_sample`, and `motion_calibration`; `<cmath>` supplies `std::fabs`, while `<algorithm>` supplies `std::max`.